{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Launch a review into protections for domestic abuse victims in the workplace",
        "additional_details": "We call on the Government to launch a review into whether stronger legal protections are needed for victims of domestic abuse, and where professional power, workplace retaliation and work-related institutions can compound suffering for victims. \r\nThe review should investigate how to protect victims when conflicts of interest arise, how to ensure victims are heard, and ensure protections from unlawful retaliation, transparent decisions and meaningful accountability when workplaces fail in their duties. No one should be above scrutiny, and no victim should be without a voice.",
        "background": "We believe the Government needs to examine whether existing legal protections work effectively when domestic abuse, professional power, employment consequences and safeguarding responsibilities intersect. Professional status should not prevent anyone from being held accountable.\r\n",
